WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:02.310
- I wanna close up the
show with one more story

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:03.143
to make you smile.

00:00:03.143 --> 00:00:04.296
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:04.296 --> 00:00:07.690
(lively music)
(audience applauding)

00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:10.200
Ernest Hemingway is
celebrated all over the world.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:13.580
Obviously, but maybe nowhere
more than in Key West, Florida,

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:15.690
where he lived in the
twenties and thirties.

00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:17.290
For 40 years, the community has held

00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:19.900
a huge Ernest Hemingway
look-alike competition.

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:22.080
More than a hundred guys
from all over the country,

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:23.990
come down to vie for the title.

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:24.900
For this year's winner,

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:26.593
the victory was extra special.

00:00:26.593 --> 00:00:30.500
He won two decades after
his late father-in-law won.

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:31.690
Which is awesome.

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:35.160
Let's say hi to the 2021 Ernest
Hemingway look-alike winner,

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:37.520
Zach, dialing in from Douglas, Georgia.

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:39.948
Where he watches us on WALB 10 at three.

00:00:39.948 --> 00:00:41.780
(Kelly claps)
(audience applauding)

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:43.290
Whats up, Zach.

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:44.230
- How are you?

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:45.100
How are you Kelly?

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:45.933
- I'm so good.

00:00:45.933 --> 00:00:47.150
I like Sloppy Joe's too.

00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:47.983
I see your shirt.

00:00:47.983 --> 00:00:51.840
The competition is a big
deal in your family, right?

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:52.673
- Yes, it is.

00:00:52.673 --> 00:00:57.030
My father-in-law won in
2000 and it's very special.

00:00:57.030 --> 00:00:59.440
We slipped down and surprised him

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:01.980
in his second year of competing in '98

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:03.610
and all had a big time.

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:04.860
And even after he won,

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:07.610
we decided we would continue to go back

00:01:07.610 --> 00:01:10.840
and support other Papas or
wannabes as we call them,

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:15.010
trying to be a Papa and
support the Look-Alike Society

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:16.704
and the good things that they try to do.

00:01:16.704 --> 00:01:19.050
It's just been a lot of fun going back,

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:22.250
and we have a big time
every year down there.

00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:23.083
- I love it.
(audience applauding)

00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:25.530
I could hear you talk all day long.

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:26.750
I love your accent.

00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:27.583
Oh my goodness.

00:01:27.583 --> 00:01:30.640
So what was it like to
take the title this year?

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:32.110
That must have been pretty cool.

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:33.729
- It was really a shock.

00:01:33.729 --> 00:01:36.460
You know, after seeing
a lot of competitions,

00:01:36.460 --> 00:01:39.090
I know it's not a sprint, it's a marathon.

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:41.750
You normally have several
years of competing,

00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:45.830
and hoping that you've proved your.

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:46.944
- Lookalike-ness?

00:01:46.944 --> 00:01:49.470
(Kelly laughs)
- Your tenacity to be a Papa.

00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:51.618
I competed my first year in 2019,

00:01:51.618 --> 00:01:55.179
and didn't have it last year
because of the pandemic.

00:01:55.179 --> 00:01:57.080
This year we went back down

00:01:57.080 --> 00:01:57.976
and you know,

00:01:57.976 --> 00:02:00.120
was just thinking, I'd be lucky again.

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:02.250
Maybe if I could make
it back to the finals

00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:03.570
on Saturday night.

00:02:03.570 --> 00:02:06.993
Was really shocked when I
made it to the final five

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:08.660
and was really shocked

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:10.770
when I made it through the three way tie

00:02:11.926 --> 00:02:13.310
for the Papa.

00:02:13.310 --> 00:02:16.371
And it's just overwhelming
and just really,

00:02:16.371 --> 00:02:20.280
really, really still enjoying the ride.

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:21.364
- Oh, that's so Cool!

00:02:21.364 --> 00:02:22.197
And I love that.

00:02:22.197 --> 00:02:25.120
It's like a family tradition
now for your family.

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:26.620
Thank you so much, Zach.

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:27.740
And congratulations.

00:02:27.740 --> 00:02:29.097
I'm liking your posts right now.

00:02:29.097 --> 00:02:30.000
(bell dings)
(audience applauding)

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.220
And that's not all, man.

00:02:31.220 --> 00:02:33.010
Our season long partner Pilot Pen,

00:02:33.010 --> 00:02:34.660
the go-to pen of the "Kelly Clarkson Show"

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:37.660
wants to honor ultimate
overachievers just like you.

00:02:37.660 --> 00:02:39.770
So they're gonna be using
their G2 jelling pen

00:02:39.770 --> 00:02:41.650
to write you a check for a $1000.

00:02:41.650 --> 00:02:42.483
How's that sound?

00:02:42.483 --> 00:02:43.520
(audience applauding)

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:45.563
- Great! Thank you so much.

00:02:45.563 --> 00:02:46.862
Thank you, thank you.

00:02:46.862 --> 00:02:48.162
- [Kelly] Absolutely, man.

